{"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Se","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SE","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SH","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/ST","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s10SetAlgebraP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Sorted-sets","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/RedBlackTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap"],"title":"Sorted sets"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/splaytree"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SplayTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A splay tree keeps no balance information. Any sequence of "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" insertions, removals and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accesses on "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" elements costs O(("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") in all, so each takes O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"amortized, and recently or frequently accessed elements stay near the root: accessing the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements in ascending order costs O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") in all. Reads ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", the bounds, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subscripts and iteration) leave the tree as it is, so they keep the value semantics and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API of the other sorted sets, and take time proportional to the element’s depth, which a run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of ascending insertions can make "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/access(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to look an element up and splay it."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var recent: SplayTree = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]","recent.access(40)             \/\/ 40, now at the root","recent.contains(25)           \/\/ false, and the tree is unchanged","let parts = recent.split(at: 30)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [10, 20]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [30, 40, 50]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The elements are a random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank like an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tree[0]"},{"type":"text","text":" is the smallest element. The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"links, so the tree holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1 elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when one copy is mutated."}]}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"BinarySearchTrees"}],"title":"SplayTree","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:17BinarySearchTrees9SplayTreeV","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree.swift#L28","fileName":"SplayTree.swift"},"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SplayTree","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SplayTree"}],"roleHeading":"Structure"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A sorted set kept in a splay tree: a binary search tree that rotates each element it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accesses, inserts or removes up to the root (Sleator and Tarjan, 1985)."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree\/Split"],"title":"Structures"},{"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Bin